00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:43.000
Prometheus basically does the central component inside Prometheus.

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:45.000
That is your time series database.

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:51.000
Prometheus goes over your target and scrapes the matrix from there.

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:57.000
And after scraping, it saves your matrix in your time series database.

00:06:58.000 --> 00:07:02.000
And using PromQL, which is Prometheus's query language.

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:08.000
Through that, you can query this database and fetch the results from here.

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:16.000
We also studied that to set up Prometheus, you have two types of components.

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:20.000
First is your client libraries.

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:23.000
Client libraries are basically your SDKs.

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:29.000
Which you get for different languages like Python, javascript, c.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:35.000
Through this, you can monitor anything in your application code.

00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:39.000
You can use client libraries to calculate any matrix.

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:47.000
We are not using client libraries because we are using LangFuse for monitoring.

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:51.000
And second is your exporters.

00:07:52.000 --> 00:07:53.000
What are exporters?

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:58.000
These are your pre-built packages which expose your matrix.

00:07:58.000 --> 00:08:06.000
And to expose our system matrix, the exporter we are using is called node exporter.

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:15.000
So if you want to expose your Linux based system, like CPU, RAM, disk, network.

00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:22.000
If you want to expose your hardware based matrix, you use pre-built exporters.

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:28.000
And exporters expose all your matrix at a particular endpoint.

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:34.000
And the speciality of that endpoint is that it always starts with the defaults and matrix.

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:44.000
So we have created our EC2 instances through the auto scaling group.

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:54.000
So what we have done here is that we have added our code to the launch template.

00:08:55.000 --> 00:08:58.000
To install node exporter.

00:08:59.000 --> 00:09:07.000
So as soon as my EC2 instance is created, it will automatically install the node exporter.

00:09:07.000 --> 00:09:14.000
And automatically the matrix of that particular machine will be exposed at this particular endpoint.

00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:18.000
Now what I have to do is that my matrix is exposed.

00:09:19.000 --> 00:09:22.000
Now I have to scrape them through Prometheus.

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:31.000
So if you want to set any target in Prometheus, on which you basically scrape the matrix, there are two ways.

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:35.000
First is you set it through static configs.

00:09:36.000 --> 00:09:41.000
And second is you set it through a service discovery.

00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:45.000
Which is also called SDB.

00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:47.000
So what is static configs?

00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:54.000
If you know the full address of your endpoint, then you can add it to this static config.

00:09:54.000 --> 00:10:03.000
But the problem is that in our auto scaling group, we are scaling up and down according to the CPU usage.

00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:10.000
So sometimes it happens that some new instances are being created and sometimes the instances that are already running are being closed.

00:10:11.000 --> 00:10:13.000
And traffic is managing our load balancer.

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:15.000
So what is here?

00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:19.000
Here we have this static config or this static address.

00:10:20.000 --> 00:10:21.000
It is not available.

00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:24.000
All the things we have are dynamic.

00:10:25.000 --> 00:10:31.000
Addresses are also dynamic and how many instances are running at the same time, all those things are happening dynamically.

00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:35.000
So we have to use another mechanism here, that is service discovery.

00:10:36.000 --> 00:10:44.000
Service discovery is made so that it can automatically track your dynamic endpoints and scrape the matrix from there.

00:10:44.000 --> 00:10:56.000
So what we did here is we set our EC2 service discovery in our YAML file, which is the config file of our Prometheus.

